body:
`needs_bump?` uses `start_with?(gem_dir)` to detect changes under a gem’s directory. This will incorrectly treat changes in similarly-prefixed gem dirs (e.g., `tools/ruby-gems/udb-gen/...` or `tools/ruby-gems/udb_helpers/...`) as changes to `tools/ruby-gems/udb` because those paths also start with `tools/ruby-gems/udb`. Use a boundary-aware check (e.g., `f == gem_dir` or `f.start_with?("#{gem_dir}/")`, ideally via `Pathname#ascend`/`fnmatch`) to avoid false positives and unintended version bumps/cascades.
```suggestion
def path_matches_dir?(path, dir)
  path == dir || path.start_with?("#{dir}/")
end

def needs_bump?(gem_config, changed_files, base_ref)
  gem_dir = gem_config[:dir]
  version_file = gem_config[:version_file]
  additional_dirs = gem_config[:additional_dirs] || []

  gem_files_changed = changed_files.any? { |f| path_matches_dir?(f, gem_dir) }
  additional_files_changed = additional_dirs.any? do |dir|
    changed_files.any? { |f| path_matches_dir?(f, dir) }
```
